  "oracles": [
    "Grant root remains pinned across chdir and trusted root rename; relative, absolute, and dirfd paths work within the grant.",
    "Parent traversal cannot escape grant, cross mounts, or follow symlinks; failed chdir preserves cwd.",
    "getcwd refuses a cwd moved outside the grant, and concurrent rename traversal never reads the outside sentinel.",
    "pipe2 validates flags and capabilities, respects O_NONBLOCK/O_CLOEXEC, preserves data/EOF/EPIPE, and rejects strict raw-register violations.",
    "Real cross-page RW/PROT_NONE faults copy the first reserved fd then fail the second copy; both remain EBADF and immediate successful retry reuses both numbers.",
    "With one free descriptor, second-fd reservation fails under Linux RLIMIT_NOFILE=32 and frontend DOM_FDS=1024; the first reservation remains reusable.",
    "Read-only metadata-count pages force failure after payload and primary reply writes; the task dies with SIGSEGV before user resumption.",
    "128 payload-copy failures and 64 metadata-copy failures per arm do not grow observed Linux file-nr; the supervisor accepts at most 16 extra files to bound counter noise, versus 256/128 references if all failed pipe pairs leaked.",
    "Linux SIGUSR1 is really ignored, caught-handler installation fails without changing that disposition, SIGUSR2 default terminates, SIGSTOP/SIGCONT stop and resume, and SIGKILL terminates."
  ],
  "scope_exclusions": [
    "No spawn, fork, exec replacement, wait, or shell service is implemented or qualified by this record.",
    "No benchmark sources or inputs were modified; no SPEC output comparison is claimed here.",
    "Caught-signal delivery, automatic syscall restart, thread cancellation, multi-threaded domains, SMP, audit/seccomp/tracing, and FPGA behavior remain outside this gate.",
    "The direct fixture explicitly selects the register pipe ABI; ordinary musl pipe2 remains exchange-based. Metadata-reply failure tests exercise the exchange ABI in both SDK builds.",
    "Finite concurrent-rename and resource-pressure tests are evidence, not an exhaustive proof of race freedom or absence of all leaks."
  ],
